# Pruebas manuales con la extensión REST Client de VS Code.
# Local: `func start` (o F5). En Azure cambiar @host y poner la clave en @key.
@host = http://localhost:7071
@key =

### Salud
GET {{host}}/api/health

### Verificado (DNI de demostración, DNI_PROVIDER=fake)
POST {{host}}/api/verify-dni
Content-Type: application/json
x-functions-key: {{key}}

{ "investorId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111", "dni": "12345678", "firstName": "Juan Carlos", "lastName": "Perez Gomez" }

### Nombres que no coinciden -> NAME_MISMATCH
POST {{host}}/api/verify-dni
Content-Type: application/json
x-functions-key: {{key}}

{ "dni": "12345678", "firstName": "Pedro", "lastName": "Ramos" }

### DNI inexistente -> NOT_FOUND
POST {{host}}/api/verify-dni
Content-Type: application/json
x-functions-key: {{key}}

{ "dni": "11111111", "firstName": "Juan", "lastName": "Perez" }

### DNI inválido -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/verify-dni
Content-Type: application/json
x-functions-key: {{key}}

{ "dni": "1234567", "firstName": "Juan", "lastName": "Perez" }

### Fuente caída (solo con DNI_PROVIDER=fake) -> 502
POST {{host}}/api/verify-dni
Content-Type: application/json
x-functions-key: {{key}}

{ "dni": "00000503", "firstName": "Juan", "lastName": "Perez" }
